===Etymology===
According to the Romanian etymological dictionary, borrowed from {{etyl|la|ro}} ''[[corpus]]'' (through a {{etyl|de|ro}} or Russian intermediate ''[[Korpus]]'' in the 18th century and {{etyl|fr|ro}} ''[[corps]]'' later in the 19th century). The Megleno-Romanian equivalent, also {{term|corp|lang=ruq}}, seems to be directly inherited from Latin, however. <ref>[http://dexonline.ro/definitie/corp Romanian Explanatory Dictionary]</ref>

